  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Authentication – We will Shib-enable Fedora, enabling a ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "user to provide credentials managed by their origin ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "institution, and providing a single sign-in solution for ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Fedora. We will obtain attributes about users ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "(Eduperson), and we will use those attributed in ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "authorization.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Authorization – we will support XML-encoded policies ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "(XACML). Fedora will constrain what can be expressed ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "in the policies to things Fedora is prepared to enforce. ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Policies can refer to user attributes, and attributes of ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Fedora digital objects. We will build the Fedora ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "authorization module to interpret and enforce policies.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Date: 2004-05-11 14:48",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
